---
pagination:
  data: synonyms.redirects
  size: 1
  alias: r
permalink: "/species/{{ r.fromSlug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ r.fromName }} → {{ r.toName }} — BeeAtlas"
---
{#- A folded name keeps its old URL and forwards to the accepted one. Built from
    the dbt synonym seeds by _data/synonyms.js; see there for why this is a meta
    refresh rather than a 301.

    Deliberately standalone — no site layout, no header, no bundle. The reader is
    here for a fraction of a second, and a page that loads the app before jumping
    would be slower than the redirect it performs. The visible text is for the
    case where the refresh does not fire (a text browser, a bot, refresh disabled)
    and for anyone who stops the load to read it. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<link rel="icon" href="data:,">
{#- canonical + a zero-delay refresh, and deliberately NO robots noindex: a
    noindex on a page that also names a canonical can propagate to the canonical
    target, which would deindex the species page this is trying to send people to. -#}
<link rel="canonical" href="https://beeatlas.net/species/{{ r.toSlug }}/index.html">
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/species/{{ r.toSlug }}/index.html">
<style>
  body { font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 4rem auto; max-width: 34rem; padding: 0 1rem; }
  em { font-style: italic; }
  .reason { color: #555; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<p><em>{{ r.fromName }}</em> is now listed as
  <a href="/species/{{ r.toSlug }}/index.html"><em>{{ r.toName }}</em></a>.</p>
<p>Redirecting; if nothing happens,
  <a href="/species/{{ r.toSlug }}/index.html">open the {{ r.toName }} page</a>.</p>
{%- if r.reason %}
<p class="reason">{{ r.reason }}</p>
{%- endif %}
</body>
</html>
